* /**
*  * @file GIT.PREFIX
*  * @version 1.0
*  */
* GIT.PREFIX(pfx) — where this account sits inside its repository, as a path
* prefix ending in "/", or "" when the account IS the repository root.
*
* A repository may hold several accounts beside ordinary files, and the paths it
* stores carry the account:
*
*     demo/.mvx                 the account marker
*     demo/BP.DICT/%FILE%       a file's control, under its account
*     demo/BP/MOUSE-DEMO        a record: <account>/<file>/<id>
*     .github/workflows/ci.yml  ordinary files, at the top
*
* MVX produces that shape without trying: with the open format its records ARE
* files in directories on disk, so git's own `add` walks them from the repo root
* and the account name is simply part of the path it finds.
*
* UniVerse and UniData have no such luck — records live in hash files and never
* appear on disk — so the verb CONSTRUCTS each path, and without this prefix it
* builds `<file>/<id>`.  For an account at the root that is right.  For an
* account below it, two accounts would both claim `CUST/C1` and overwrite each
* other, and a checkout could not tell whose record it was holding.
      SUBROUTINE GIT.PREFIX(PFX)
      $INCLUDE BP.INC PLATFORM.H
      PFX = ""
      $IFDEF MVX
*     MVX has no @PATH to compare against a root, and needs none: in session the
*     account is the working directory and therefore the repository itself, so
*     there is no prefix.  Where several accounts DO share one repository — the
*     mvx-git CLI walking them — the engine sets its own prefix in C, at the one
*     boundary where a record's git path is built.
      RETURN
      $ENDIF
      REPO = ""
      CALL GIT.REPO(REPO)
*     GIT.REPO returns "<root>/.git"; the root is that with the suffix removed.
      L = LEN(REPO)
      IF L < 6 THEN RETURN
      IF REPO[L-4, 5] # "/.git" THEN RETURN
      ROOT = REPO[1, L-5]
      ACCT = @PATH
*     The account IS the root: no prefix, and the paths stay as they always were.
      IF ACCT = ROOT THEN RETURN
      RL = LEN(ROOT)
      IF LEN(ACCT) <= RL + 1 THEN RETURN
      IF ACCT[1, RL] # ROOT THEN RETURN      ;* not below the root after all
      IF ACCT[RL+1, 1] # "/" THEN RETURN     ;* a sibling whose name merely starts the same
      PFX = ACCT[RL+2, LEN(ACCT)-RL-1] : "/"
      RETURN
      END

